<div class="probe-dump-path">
  <style>
    .probe-dump-path { margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    .probe-dump-path h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
    .probe-dump-path table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .9rem; }
    .probe-dump-path th, .probe-dump-path td { border: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,.35); padding: .35rem .6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
    .probe-dump-path code { font-family: ui-monospace, Consolas, monospace; }
    .probe-dump-path .miss { color: #b3261e; font-weight: 600; }
    .probe-dump-path .hit { color: #1b7f3b; font-weight: 600; }
    .probe-dump-path p { font-size: .85rem; margin: .5rem 0 0; }
  </style>
  <h3>Finding 1 — the dump path the help names against the path the binary writes</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th><code>--ticks-out</code> value</th><th>Help text promises (<code>&lt;FILE&gt;.jsonl</code>)</th><th>Binary wrote</th><th>Match</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>match.ticks</code></td><td><code>match.ticks.jsonl</code></td><td><code>match.jsonl</code></td><td class="miss">differs</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>two.dots.bin</code></td><td><code>two.dots.bin.jsonl</code></td><td><code>two.dots.jsonl</code></td><td class="miss">differs</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>noext</code></td><td><code>noext.jsonl</code></td><td><code>noext.jsonl</code></td><td class="hit">equal</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>s42-1m.ticks</code> (first drive)</td><td><code>s42-1m.ticks.jsonl</code></td><td><code>s42-1m.jsonl</code></td><td class="miss">differs</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Rule observed: the binary replaces the last extension with <code>.jsonl</code>. The help text holds only when the tick path has no extension. Evidence: <code>probe-evidence/engine-core/reobs-json-path.listing.txt</code>.</p>
</div>
